{"dur":555,"ev":[{"t":3,"type":"voice","id":"n01","dlg":false,"sub":"Every morning, a mirror shows you who you are."},{"t":7.4,"type":"voice","id":"n02","dlg":false,"sub":"One Tuesday, Theo’s mirror showed him who he was going to be."},{"t":13.4,"type":"voice","id":"t01","dlg":true,"sub":"Wait. What?","who":"Theo"},{"t":17.6,"type":"voice","id":"t02","dlg":true,"sub":"Hello? Hey!","who":"Theo"},{"t":21.6,"type":"voice","id":"n03","dlg":false,"sub":"The man in the glass was ten years older. And he wasn’t copying him."},{"t":39.2,"type":"voice","id":"n04","dlg":false,"sub":"He did what anyone would do. He tested it."},{"t":43,"type":"voice","id":"t03","dlg":true,"sub":"Left hand.","who":"Theo"},{"t":46,"type":"voice","id":"n05","dlg":false,"sub":"The reflection followed. A moment too late."},{"t":50.4,"type":"voice","id":"n06","dlg":false,"sub":"Every face in a mirror is a little out of date."},{"t":53.8,"type":"voice","id":"n07","dlg":false,"sub":"Stand a metre from the glass, and the light takes about seven billionths of a second to come back to you."},{"t":62.8,"type":"voice","id":"n08","dlg":false,"sub":"Theo’s mirror was ten years out. In the wrong direction."},{"t":67.3,"type":"voice","id":"n09","dlg":false,"sub":"Same nose. Less hair. Tired eyes. An office badge."},{"t":72.9,"type":"voice","id":"n10","dlg":false,"sub":"His cello, shut and dusty. And on the wall, an audition poster. Crossed out."},{"t":81,"type":"voice","id":"t04","dlg":true,"sub":"Okay. Phone camera.","who":"Theo"},{"t":84.4,"type":"voice","id":"t05","dlg":true,"sub":"Normal. Totally normal.","who":"Theo"},{"t":89,"type":"voice","id":"n11","dlg":false,"sub":"The hall mirror was normal too. Only the bathroom one knew."},{"t":100.8,"type":"voice","id":"t06","dlg":true,"sub":"Nan, does your mirror ever show you older?","who":"Theo"},{"t":105,"type":"voice","id":"a01","dlg":true,"sub":"Every morning, love. It’s called being seventy-eight.","who":"Nan"},{"t":110,"type":"voice","id":"t07","dlg":true,"sub":"No, I mean ten years older. And he looked like he’d given up.","who":"Theo"},{"t":115.4,"type":"voice","id":"a02","dlg":true,"sub":"Given up on what?","who":"Nan"},{"t":118,"type":"voice","id":"t08","dlg":true,"sub":"On me. He gave up on me.","who":"Theo"},{"t":121.6,"type":"voice","id":"a03","dlg":true,"sub":"Then he’s a stranger, love. You haven’t met him yet.","who":"Nan"},{"t":127.6,"type":"voice","id":"n12","dlg":false,"sub":"Psychologists asked over nineteen thousand people how much they’d change in the next ten years."},{"t":134.4,"type":"voice","id":"n13","dlg":false,"sub":"Not much, they said. But people ten years older said they’d changed a lot."},{"t":140,"type":"voice","id":"n14","dlg":false,"sub":"We always think we’re nearly finished. It’s called the end of history illusion."},{"t":151.4,"type":"voice","id":"n15","dlg":false,"sub":"The next morning, the man was still there."},{"t":158.4,"type":"voice","id":"n16","dlg":false,"sub":"On the way to work, Theo saw the poster from the mirror."},{"t":163.6,"type":"voice","id":"n17","dlg":false,"sub":"Port Alder Orchestra. Auditions. In seventy days."},{"t":168.8,"type":"voice","id":"t09","dlg":true,"sub":"Seventy days.","who":"Theo"},{"t":175.8,"type":"voice","id":"n18","dlg":false,"sub":"He walked to work. The next morning, the man in the glass stood a little straighter."},{"t":182.6,"type":"voice","id":"n19","dlg":false,"sub":"That night, he opened the cello for the first time in two years."},{"t":193,"type":"voice","id":"t10","dlg":true,"sub":"Sorry! Sorry.","who":"Theo"},{"t":196,"type":"voice","id":"n20","dlg":false,"sub":"He was rusty. And seventy days is not very long."},{"t":202.4,"type":"voice","id":"n21","dlg":false,"sub":"In the glass, the man had stopped looking at him."},{"t":206.6,"type":"voice","id":"t11","dlg":true,"sub":"Hey. Hey! Look at me!","who":"Theo"},{"t":213,"type":"voice","id":"n22","dlg":false,"sub":"Here’s the strange part. When people imagine themselves in ten years, their brains respond a bit like they’re thinking about a stranger."},{"t":222.2,"type":"voice","id":"n23","dlg":false,"sub":"In one experiment, people who met an aged picture of themselves set aside more than twice as much for retirement."},{"t":230.6,"type":"voice","id":"n24","dlg":false,"sub":"Theo didn’t have a picture. He had a witness. And the witness was losing hope."},{"t":241,"type":"voice","id":"n25","dlg":false,"sub":"New habits take about sixty-six days, on average, to become automatic."},{"t":246.4,"type":"voice","id":"n26","dlg":false,"sub":"Some take eighteen. Some take over two hundred. Theo had sixty-four."},{"t":262.6,"type":"voice","id":"n27","dlg":false,"sub":"Six days before the audition, he took the cello up to the roof."},{"t":287.2,"type":"voice","id":"a04","dlg":true,"sub":"Not bad at all, love!","who":"Nan"},{"t":294.4,"type":"voice","id":"t12","dlg":true,"sub":"Nan? Nan!","who":"Theo"},{"t":308.6,"type":"voice","id":"n28","dlg":false,"sub":"Three days before the audition, the mirror showed the bathroom. Just the bathroom."},{"t":314.8,"type":"voice","id":"t13","dlg":true,"sub":"Hello?","who":"Theo"},{"t":317.4,"type":"voice","id":"t14","dlg":true,"sub":"Where are you?","who":"Theo"},{"t":320.4,"type":"voice","id":"n29","dlg":false,"sub":"No man. No office badge. Not even the cello. Ten years from now, nobody lived here."},{"t":330.6,"type":"voice","id":"t15","dlg":true,"sub":"He’s gone. The one in the mirror is gone.","who":"Theo"},{"t":334.7,"type":"voice","id":"a05","dlg":true,"sub":"Gone where, love?","who":"Nan"},{"t":337.6,"type":"voice","id":"t16","dlg":true,"sub":"I don’t know. And I’m not going to Port Alder. Not with you like this.","who":"Theo"},{"t":343,"type":"voice","id":"a06","dlg":true,"sub":"Don’t you dare stay for me. Did you look properly?","who":"Nan"},{"t":357.4,"type":"voice","id":"n30","dlg":false,"sub":"He hadn’t vanished. He’d moved out."},{"t":361,"type":"voice","id":"t17","dlg":true,"sub":"Port Alder.","who":"Theo"},{"t":364.6,"type":"voice","id":"n31","dlg":false,"sub":"Tucked in the frame was a postcard from the sea. In his own handwriting."},{"t":370.6,"type":"voice","id":"n32","dlg":false,"sub":"The future hadn’t ended. It had moved. But only if he went."},{"t":394.6,"type":"voice","id":"n33","dlg":false,"sub":"He had one more night. He played until his fingers hurt."},{"t":421.2,"type":"voice","id":"n34","dlg":false,"sub":"On the last morning, Theo didn’t check the mirror."},{"t":425.4,"type":"voice","id":"n35","dlg":false,"sub":"He had seen enough to start."},{"t":433.4,"type":"voice","id":"a07","dlg":true,"sub":"Go on, love. And send me a postcard.","who":"Nan"},{"t":437.4,"type":"voice","id":"t18","dlg":true,"sub":"I think I already did.","who":"Theo"},{"t":451,"type":"voice","id":"n36","dlg":false,"sub":"The train left at six. The audition was at nine."},{"t":466.6,"type":"voice","id":"p01","dlg":true,"sub":"Whenever you’re ready.","who":"Panel"},{"t":478.9,"type":"voice","id":"p02","dlg":true,"sub":"Would you like to stop?","who":"Panel"},{"t":482.2,"type":"voice","id":"t19","dlg":true,"sub":"No. I’m not stopping.","who":"Theo"},{"t":489.9,"type":"voice","id":"p03","dlg":true,"sub":"Thank you. We’ll be in touch.","who":"Panel"},{"t":496,"type":"voice","id":"n37","dlg":false,"sub":"And they were."},{"t":509.6,"type":"voice","id":"n38","dlg":false,"sub":"Ten years later, in a flat by the sea, a man stepped up to a mirror."},{"t":515.2,"type":"voice","id":"n39","dlg":false,"sub":"It showed him at forty-four. And this time, the man in the glass waved first."},{"t":522,"type":"voice","id":"t20","dlg":true,"sub":"Hi, you.","who":"Theo"},{"t":526,"type":"voice","id":"n40","dlg":false,"sub":"He didn’t ask what he’d become. He knew the trick now. It gets decided every morning."},{"t":12.950000000000001,"type":"chime"},{"t":17.150000000000002,"type":"chime"},{"t":42.55,"type":"chime"},{"t":80.55,"type":"chime"},{"t":83.95,"type":"chime"},{"t":100.35,"type":"chime"},{"t":104.55,"typ